# Line-ending policy (installed by nissth-init; mirrors the Nissth framework's own).
#
# LF baseline pinned in-tree so a clone on a host with core.autocrlf=true does not
# CRLF-convert markdown, fixtures, or launchers. See the Nissth Report
# AgentReports/Reports/2026-08-21_fresh-clone-build-failures.md for the defect
# this prevents.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files must keep CRLF (LF-only .cmd files misparse labels/goto on Windows).
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Deliberately NOT overridden: *.ps1 and the extensionless POSIX launcher —
# both read LF correctly and the launcher must stay executable on macOS/Linux.

# Never run text filters over binaries.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
